.TH DOTMORPH 1 "2026-10-24" "DotMorph 2.0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dotmorph \- convert files from a radial menu, the file manager or the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dotmorph
[\fB\-\-theme\fR \fIdark|light|glass\fR] [\fB\-\-reduce\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-clipboard\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-daemon\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B dotmorph
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
DotMorph converts images, PDF, SVG, video, audio, Office documents and Markdown using the tools installed on the system (Pillow, librsvg, poppler, Ghostscript, ImageMagick, ffmpeg, LibreOffice, pandoc). Without a command it opens the radial menu for the given files; through the daemon this takes about 0.1 s.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBconvert\fR
Convert files from the terminal.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fITARGET\fR
format (png, mp4, pdf, ...) or tool: compress, resize\-50, rotate\-90, strip, mute, merge\-pdf
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fIPRESET\fR
web: WebP, fits 1920x1920, quality 80, no metadata; email: JPG, fits 1280x1280, quality 75, no metadata; thumb: WebP thumbnail, fits 320x320; print: high resolution: PDF/SVG at 300 dpi, quality 95; share: smaller file in the same format, no metadata
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fIOUT\fR
output directory (default: next to source)
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-dpi\fR \fIDPI\fR
render resolution (default: PDF 150, SVG 96 = original size)
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-quality\fR \fIQUALITY\fR
JPEG/WebP/AVIF quality (default 90)
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-resize\fR \fISPEC\fR
50%, 1920x1080 (fit inside) or 1280 (width)
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-strip\fR
drop EXIF / tags while converting
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-overwrite\fR
replace existing files
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIJOBS\fR
files converted in parallel (default: CPU cores, up to 8)
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fITIMEOUT\fR
give up on one file after N seconds
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
no progress bar
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-notify\fR
desktop notification when done (with an Open folder button)
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
show what would be converted, and how, without doing it
.RE
.TP
\fBformats\fR
List supported conversions.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-missing\fR
what installing the missing tools would add
.RE
.TP
\fBsettings\fR
Open the settings window.
.TP
\fBcompletions\fR
Shell completion script (bash, zsh, fish).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-install\fR
write it where your shell picks it up (per user)
.RE
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Check which tools are installed and what they unlock.
.TP
\fBdaemon\fR
Keep the wheel loaded so it opens instantly.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-install\fR
start now and at every login
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-uninstall\fR
stop and remove from login
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\fR
stop the running daemon
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR
is it running?
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fITHEME\fR
override the theme from the settings
.RE
.TP
\fBintegrate\fR
Add DotMorph to file\-manager right\-click menus and Open With.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\fR
take everything out again
.RE
.TP
\fBhotkey\fR
Global shortcut: open the wheel with the copied files.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fIKEY\fR
e.g. '<Super><Shift>m' (the default) or '<Control><Alt>c'
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
even if the key is already taken
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\fR
remove the shortcut
.RE
.TP
\fBwatch\fR
Convert new files in folders automatically.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fITARGET\fR
format or tool for new files
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fIEXTS\fR
only these source formats, comma separated (default: all that fit)
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fIOUT\fR
output directory (default: same folder)
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-quality\fR \fIQUALITY\fR

.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-resize\fR \fISPEC\fR

.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-strip\fR

.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-recursive\fR
watch sub\-folders too
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-notify\fR
notification for each file
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-install\fR
run as a systemd user service
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
list installed watch services
.RE
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-uninstall\fR \fINAME\fR
remove an installed watch service
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/dotmorph/settings.json\fR
Theme, language, options, pinned and hidden formats, edge dock position.
.TP
\fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dotmorph.sock\fR
The daemon's socket.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBDOTMORPH_THEME\fR
dark, light or glass; overrides the saved theme.
.TP
\fBDOTMORPH_REDUCE_MOTION\fR
1 turns the wheel's animations off.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when everything converted, 1 when something failed, 130 when cancelled.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dotmorph photo.png
dotmorph convert report.pdf \-\-to png \-\-dpi 200
dotmorph convert holiday.mov \-\-to mp4
dotmorph convert shots/*.png \-\-preset web
dotmorph watch ~/Downloads \-\-from heic \-\-to jpg \-\-install
dotmorph doctor
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBffmpeg\fR(1), \fBpdftoppm\fR(1), \fBgs\fR(1), \fBmagick\fR(1), \fBpandoc\fR(1)
.PP
